<title>AZERBAIJAN: Azerbaijan oil output to hit 13.5 mln T/yr by 2000.</title>
<headline>Azerbaijan oil output to hit 13.5 mln T/yr by 2000.</headline>
<dateline>BAKU 1997-04-03</dateline>
<text>
<p>Annual crude oil output in the former Soviet republic of Azerbaijan will rise to 13.5 million tonnes, or 270,000 barrels per day, by 2000, state oil company SOCAR said on Thursday.</p>
<p>Production would more than triple to 45 million tonnes (900,000 bpd) by 2010, once large projects in the Azeri sector of the Caspian Sea reach peak production levels.</p>
<p>Total output last year was 9.0 million tonnes (180,000 bpd).</p>
<p>--Moscow Newsroom, +7095 941 8520</p>
</text>
